<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The corpse blobs are being partially controlled by the finnwoman, whose name is Triemides. She is able to remotely control some aspects of the corpses, mostly relating to the subliminal messaging and communication attempts via the carvings on various objects. She's using this to send cries for help in whatever way she can, due to the fact that she's losing a 5000 year fight against Teran, partially because of human inflicted damage on the sites that the corpse blobs are located at. This is seen at the end of the SCP. As for the purpose of the corpse balls themselves, they are holding open a trans-planar tunnel which is being used to power my 001.</p>
<p>It's implied at the end that Alva is not actually who she seems to be. In Orcadian myth, there is a deity know as The Mither o' Sea, and another Deity known as Teran. They fight an endless cycle of dominance with one another (A theme which is heavily prevalent in 3700) and this is another piece where that theme is coming into play. Alva, is the Mither in human form, and the Fishwoman's message at the end reveals this, and the large humanoid entity is Teran.</p>
<p>There are two themes running in this piece, which consist of Triemides desperation, and the sacrifices that the Finnfolk made to keep this and 5 other deities sealed (I.E. literally sacrificing themselves in large numbers to accomplish this goal.)</p>
