															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/petrograd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(455145); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=455145&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606447353" alt="Petrograd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=455145)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/petrograd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(455145); return false;" >Petrograd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1507300463 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Oct 2017 14:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3608580">
									

<p>There are a lot of things I deeply enjoy about this (e.g., the mental image of 3703/the finfolk, the implications about Alva/history/the Foundation, the carved dialogue, the mythological beasts), and some things that didn't engage me much (the war of the Gods), but there are two major problems that&#8230; honestly are leading me all the way to a downvote.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First, the description is a mess. The base anomaly is thoroughly complicated, and not broken down in a clear and understandable manner. I had to read the entire article and then reread the description twice before I got the full picture.<br />
- Describing 3703s as structures <em>before</em> talking about the structure they are found in (dash1) gave me the complete wrong initial mental image.<br />
- Describing their geometric/thaumaturgical shape and the presence of extradimensional portals, THEN their ability to interact with things, THEN the plasma generation caused confusion about what was important to know/remember, as did not designating the plasma with a letter or number.<br />
- (Also having both -A and -1 was&#8230; not a major problem, but it didn't help me zoning out a couple paragraphs in, especially as the list of effects stacked higher and higher.)<br />
- It feels like a lot of the effects (the manipulating appendages and cognitohazards especially) were basically typed in in the order that they showed up in the later story, and thus it feels like they had too much detail or were largely superfluous. Yes, the Foundation would document them like you have, but you aren't the Foundation, and you've got a bigger story to tell.</p>
<p>Second big problem was Document A. This was a <em>gigantic</em> failure of show-don't-tell, and left me rolling my eyes for the entire duration. It was basically an attempt to explain the entire premise to the reader, and isn't even remotely an interesting interpretation. I would've been far happier with my own theories.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Look&#8230; this is already a decadent exercise in rich, mythological storytelling, using a complex narrative with many subtle references. That is absolutely <em>not</em> a problem, but you can't afford to do both that and be indulgent or loose in other areas. -1</p>
<p>Improving the description would get me a fair distance towards upvoting.</p>

							</div>

								
					
