					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ankhananku" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1964779); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1964779&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606447353" alt="AnkhAnanku" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1964779)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ankhananku" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1964779); return false;" >AnkhAnanku</a></span> <span class="odate time_1507331030 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Oct 2017 23:03</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3608803">
									

<p>I agree with Petrograd above me, and have painstakingly developed a comprehensive list of why this gets my -1. Please take this as constructive criticism. Also, I may have a collapsable addiction&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Object&nbsp;Class:&nbsp;Thaumiel</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">should&nbsp;be&nbsp;nerfed&nbsp;to&nbsp;euclid</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Finnlady is your keter, and whatever was hidden in the nebula is potentially a Thaumial level threat, but the gates? Not even close to keter. While not completely understood and probably needs some TLC, there is not a scrap of evidence of the immediate keter-level threat until the reactivation log, which changes things so dramatically that we would already be in a thaumial level situation, which makes the following containment (secrecy) procedures and coy anomaly-probing close to irrelevent.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h4><span>Containment</span></h4>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Experimentation</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Not&nbsp;sure&nbsp;how&nbsp;I&nbsp;feel&nbsp;about&nbsp;that&nbsp;word</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Testing clearance should be lowered. From what we've seen, the Foundation either understands it and knows how to repair it or it doesn't and is going to keep throwing subjects and sensors at it. Further attempts to communicate with the entity should be a top priority, as is the nature the secondary and teritary anomalous effects. This is certainly worth a few D-class.</p>
<p>Since going inside, though, these things seem like they might be a waste of time or under even heavier lockdown.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">CCTV&nbsp;Cameras</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">can't&nbsp;be&nbsp;used</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Not to moniter a skip giving off visual cognitohazards, anyway. I'd lose the visual component of the hazard anyway, since a pile of corpses spelling things with their fingers is just silly. In fact, it just made me angry when it was expunged because whatever it was would have to be described vaguely anyway, which would already remove the hazard. If whatever it was were still potent after that degree of seperation, it would be a &quot;memetic.&quot; That said, I could totally see how the whisper-choreographed bone dance would be deeply unsettling.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">VERITAS</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Vital&nbsp;Energy&nbsp;Radiation&nbsp;Imaging&nbsp;Tactical&nbsp;Awareness&nbsp;System</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Had no idea what these were. I'm surprised I haven't looked into the GOC that much. That said, professional documents spell out acronyms the first time they are used in the instance. Also, they wouldn't be &quot;VERITAS readings,&quot; they'd using VERITAS to read Aetheric Energy Fields (AEF), or Elan Vital Energy (EVE), so it's &quot;changes in baseline AEF or EVE&quot; that they'd be looking for.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h4><span>Description</span></h4>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Naming&nbsp;Order</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...&nbsp;is&nbsp;just&nbsp;my&nbsp;personal&nbsp;preference</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCPs should be named by order of discovered layers: SCP-3703 should be the chamber, as it contains all the things you have to worry about. This includes the corpse jello, the whispers, the cold fire, and the Gigeresque tubes. SCP-3703-1 would be the most important item, but I should think one would designate the mana burn-off as a part of the skip which seems to be escaping containment at an alarming rate and no-one seems to have tried to analyse what it is or where it goes.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">These&nbsp;Numbers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...don't&nbsp;add&nbsp;up</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The initial containment protocol establishes there are 6 sites with a total of 13 instances of floating fish people. Shortly thereafter it becomes hundreds of structures. It just doesn't tell the right story.</p>
<p>I'd stick with six, but I'll explain that in my last suggestion.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">The&nbsp;Symbol</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...is&nbsp;just&nbsp;too&nbsp;much</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>On top of whether or not they are floating or the dimensions of the mass, the bodies are arranged in the shape of a protective seal, sigil, or glyph. Personally, I find this makes the whole thing just way too complicated. I mean now you gotta account for scale and the size of the bodies and the thickness of the lines and how many bodies can you glue together to get a reasonably legible consistency and whether or not the shapes are contiguous and I don't need to be worrying about all that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Auditory&nbsp;Stimuli</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...got&nbsp;forgotten?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It doesn't seem like audio-stimus reaction ever comes into play, either in the experiment logs or otherwise. Also, &quot;emulating&quot; might not be the right word. Overall, I'd cut it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Physical&nbsp;Stimuli</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...isn't&nbsp;too&nbsp;bad</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It's just worded painfully: no non-physical objects were presented, nor is there much difference between them and the animated drone later, so just shorten it to &quot;Items placed within 3m of SCP-3703 result in the extension of corpses to form appendages to gasp, examine, and manipulate these foreign objects before briefly internalizing them.&quot;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Plasma</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...is&nbsp;curious</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Though I can't be certain this is it's <em>purpose</em>, per se, the strange mists, vapors, and low-energy plasmas (like swamp gas and willow-the-whisps) venting off this thing are intriguing if not worrysome. There is no way we could have gotten that close to the thing without first sampling the air to see if it was breathable or figure out what that cold fire was.<br />
And sorry to get technical, but there is no &quot;energy generation&quot; going on here. It is colder than ambient, which means thermal energy has been removed. That energy may have gone into turning the vapor into a plasma, but then it would give that energy off when you touched it, and this is fiction so screw the thermodynamics, I just have an issue whether fishlady is venting or if these things are supposed to be her batteries in which case it's going the wrong way&#8230;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h4><span>Experiments and Exploration</span></h4>
<p>These were all pretty good&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Experiments</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...I&nbsp;liked</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I feel like an obscure runic text from an unknown culture are too easily translated, but whatevs<br />
The square peg without a square hole was too much fun! Almost got my upvote there.<br />
The part with the mice was good; I appreciate you not wasting D-class (who were well written, btw).<br />
Nice work with the retrieval cables, too. So many researchers forget those. Basically, I think this section is really good.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Exploration</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...was&nbsp;a&nbsp;little&nbsp;purple</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The roboticist working with Dr. Alva is obviously having way too much fun. I'm all for an irrepressible engineer, but there was no way of knowing there wouldn't be gravity in there, so going ahead and giving the drone jet thrusters made no sense. I mean what are they? Compressed air? Ion repulsors? Either way that is a substancial weight that no sane explorer would throw on a drone that has to explore an unknown distance on limited energy supplies. Maybe saying this was developed ahead of time in preparation for dodging the skip's grabby hands might justify it, particularly if that limited supply had enough left over to set it drifting down that tunnel. There should also probably be an adjustment period as the pilot discovers there is no gravity, which would completely disrupt the drone's ability to fly.</p>
<p>I'm not sure we need to know the colors of all the things. That said, when did the plasma turn into purple fluid? This might just be a problem with my headcanon, but plasma glows like lightning, like fire, like balls of blue-white energy rolling around the roof of your microwave before popping violently. &quot;Purple fluid&quot; is not that. Purple fluid sounds like a bunch of rancid wine is pooring down this well to drip down on gillgirl.</p>
<p>We know what space looks like. Don't describe it to us.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Document&nbsp;A&nbsp;and&nbsp;Reactivation&nbsp;Log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">**NOPE**</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content"></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">FINAL&nbsp;WORD</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;hope&nbsp;you&nbsp;actually&nbsp;listen&nbsp;to&nbsp;me...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I can currently only vote you down once and ultimately the moste you can get out of me is a two vote swing, so you don't have to listen to me tear your baby a new one, but I really am trying to help.</p>
<p>I honestly think you should play off som parallels with the Sarkic Cult vs CotBG mythos, particularly <a href="/scp-2688">SCP-2688</a>. The corporeal thaumaturgy, primordial sea goddesses, the <strong>six</strong> Archons&#8230;<br />
This somehow fits into established mythology, whether by another perspective or through another culture, I see a parallel waiting to be fulfilled.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
