<p>Jesus. I mean, it's not as if there weren't established standards for those sort of things already, so that the devs had to make their own completely idiosyncratic version from scratch&#8230; <em>oh wait</em></p>
<p><sub>(I hate Markdown as a wholly unnecessary anti-innovation at the best of times, like, when it actually works in a straightforward manner, because it messes up all kinds of typical online text emphasis and text char formatting conventions. When it's malfunctioning, I want to feed someone their own face)</sub></p>
<p>And it wasn't even getting <em>multiple</em> line breaks that was the issue. I couldn't get <em>any</em>. The two sentences running-on into each other that I had originally, without even a character space between them, were meant to be on wholly separate lines with whitespace between them. For some reason, it chose to completely ignore the CR/LFs for just that one part of the text.</p>

